commit 74942e1dafc45b786c5151f293b972d1a85c4902
Author:     Dennis Dyall Wallin <dennis@dyallo.se>
AuthorDate: Wed Nov 4 16:27:15 2026 +0100
Commit:     Dennis Dyall Wallin <dennis@dyallo.se>
CommitDate: Wed Nov 4 16:27:15 2026 +0100

    feat(piv)!: align key vocabulary and session-owned operation workflows
    
    Use standalone Features, Slot, and shared Core KeyType with explicit PIV wire mappings. Preserve unknown slot algorithms and complete raw metadata while rejecting malformed required fields.
    
    Enforce key, policy, and operation compatibility in the session. Move authentication prerequisites, retry fallback, PIN-only workflows, and management-key state transitions into session ownership; keep protocol helpers shallow and clear owned authentication and crypto buffers.
    
    Migrate examples, CLI consumers, API baselines, and tests. Replace callback-driven workflow tests with session/backend protocol and cleanup regressions.
    
    BREAKING CHANGE: replace PivSlot/PivFeatures/PivAlgorithm with Slot/Features/Core KeyType; slot metadata now exposes nullable KeyType, RawAlgorithmId, and RawData.

